"""upd_status.py: prepend the G1q2 entries to xr_qi/STATUS.md and xr_qs/STATUS.md (run from work/re/src; keeps the file's line endings)"""
import sys

QI_FIRST = "# xr_qi - PARTIAL (351 of 371 functions byte-identical in the real Kleaf build + compare_ko_v2 strict, G1q2: 20 differ, was 26; no stub left; kCFI preambles 346 identical; objects 264 PASS (were 33 failing), exports 14 PASS (10 CRCs forged by GENKSYMS pads), imports 118 PASS, modinfo PASS; still FAIL: function-set (5 per-TU static copies get/put_task_struct, iter_ptrs_*), 14 function relocs, 1 anon-data (iter_qos_inherit jump-table case order), jump-table, .altinstructions 697 of 700, metadata buildmeta/depends = forged). COMMUNITY-ONLY: never flash / never in a ROM build"

QI_SECTION = """
## G1q2 (18.10.2026) - real bugs found by the multiset diff, structural fixes (first line updated; COMMUNITY-ONLY, DO NOT LOAD / flash)
Tooling: `g1q2_tools/` (kk.sh = real Kleaf build + strict compare + opb multiset diff of named functions, ms.sh = one line per differing function, vk.sh = normalised diff, line_var.sh = one-line variant tester, rawf.sh, stubinv.py). Scratch <work-dir> package `re/xr_qi_g1q2` (builds take 12 s when the bazel server is free, longer in a queue: the bazel server is shared with other agents).
- **REAL BEHAVIOUR FIXES (stock semantics, not codegen)**: (1) `android_vh_rwsem_read_trylock_failed`: the barge-in retry of the read trylock is BOUNDED, at most 3 cmpxchg attempts (the stock has 3 unrolled ll/sc+casa copies); ours looped until the count had a writer bit: 38 -> 6 multiset diff (330 vs 331 insns). (2) `qi_vh_mutex_register`: the stock IGNORES the result of the first hook (`record_mutex_lock_starttime`); the first-error-wins chain starts with `mutex_unlock_slowpath`: now identical (was 19 diff, 3 extra insns). (3) `get_task_qi` / `get_alloc_task_qi` / `update_dyn_vip_prio` / free_task / task_exit used `smp_load_acquire`, the stock uses `READ_ONCE` (with CONFIG_LTO: `ldar` + LDAPR alternative + .altinstructions entry): +9 alternative sites, all `ldapr` multiset diffs gone.
- **STRUCTURAL FIXES**: (4) `trace_xr_qi.h` TRACE_EVENT blocks reordered to the stock `__event_*` address order (qi_set_qos, get_qos_by_tid, get_qos_by_pid, ..., qos_mutex_opt_spin, qos_mutex_wait, qos_rwsem_opt_rspin, qos_rwsem_wait, gpu_*, fuse, rcu, reader_retry_lock): the `event_qi_*` objects embed the `.ref.data+N` offset of their event_class, so 33 objects differed; now `objects` PASS (264), function-relocs 52 -> 14, `__bpf_raw_tp_map` equal. (5) all `qi_vh_*_register` + init_module chains are written `if ((err < 0) & !ret) ret = err;` (non-short-circuit `&` puts `ret` first in the ccmp chain exactly like the stock; `!ret && err < 0` / `err < 0 && !ret` / ternaries give the other order or a different dataflow): the 8 register functions are identical except `init_module` (4 diff: same chain inside the unrolled loop, 6 variants tried, the ret/err operand order stays swapped; documented, moved on). (6) `android_vh_percpu_rwsem_wq_add` (was 15): `unlikely(w->private != cur)` removes the extra branch/epilogue copy: 455 vs 455 insns, 12 diff = 10 call-name artefacts (`.text+N` local copies) + 1 pre-indexed `ldr x24,[x25,#0x48]!` (stock) vs `add`+`ldr` (ours) and the register naming that follows from it (tried: head computed after the load, no change). No functional difference left.
- **qos_event_handler** (diff 2, unchanged): only the cold error-block placement (EEXIST/-EINVAL tails); not retried.
- **Remaining 20 differing functions (all codegen: RA/layout, no known semantic gap)**: __qi_set_task_qos 8 (csel/cset forms of the SET/UNSET/RESTORE selection), qi_set_async_binder 12 (frame 0x70 vs 0x60), binder_set_priority 14 (frame 0x90 vs 0x80), alter_rwsem_list_add 16 (owner/cur register swap x24/x25, `w->handoff_set` through `w` vs `first`), clear_rwsem_reader_owned 9 (naming artefacts of the per-TU copies), do_qos_inherit 7 (prio spill slot), futex_wait_queue_start 7 (`and #0xffff; cmp` vs `cmp uxth`), read_trylock_failed 6 (wait_lock pointer and qos spilled to the stack in the stock), qi_acquire_gpu_blockeds 5 (the stock hoists `max-1` and exits with the pre-increment compare; 3 spellings tried, LFTR keeps the post-increment form), fuse_request_fetch 5 (`cmn #0xfff; b.hs` vs `cmn #1,lsl#12; b.hi`), android_vh_rwsem_opt_rspin 4, get_alloc_task_qi 3 (the stock keeps the early return as its own epilogue copy), undo_qos_inherit 3 (`bic` vs `and`+`mvn`), iter_binder_qos_inherit 3, init_module 4, qos_event_handler 2, plus iter_*_qos_inherit / hook functions at 1-2 (call-name artefacts of the local copies). The 5 absent functions (`get_task_struct#2`, `iter_ptrs_start#2`, `iter_ptrs_end#2`, `put_task_struct#2/#3`) are per-TU static copies: the stock has 8+ source files (binder, percpu_rwsem, rwsem, ...), ours has 3 TUs; only a split of qi_hooks.c per feature would create them (risk: inline decisions change; not done).
- Cosmetic, unchanged: qi.c messages use the prefix `qi: `, the stock strings are `qi_stats: ...` (qos_event_handler already) and `qi_utils:` (comm group). Hack list unchanged (10 forged export CRCs, `noinline` helpers, callsite `always_inline` / `__noinline__` hints). Nothing tested on a device.
"""

QS_FIRST = "# xr_qs - PARTIAL (114 of 120 functions byte-identical in the real Kleaf build + compare_ko_v2 strict; G1q2: qos_set_callback 493/439 -> 400/399 insns (multiset diff 52 -> 2), a REAL missing trace call added; function set 120 PASS, kCFI 110 identical, binding PASS, objects 114 PASS, imports 55 + exports 0 PASS, modinfo PASS, .altinstructions now 252 = 252; still FAIL: 6 function bodies (5 relocs), 1 anon-data (set_rtg_grp switch table), jump-table, metadata buildmeta/depends = forged). COMMUNITY-ONLY: never flash / never in a ROM build"

QS_SECTION = """
## G1q2 (18.10.2026) - qos_set_callback is semantically complete now (first line updated; COMMUNITY-ONLY)
- **REAL semantic fix (qos_set_callback, rt branch `(qos & 0xf) == 9`)**: after `sched_setscheduler_nocheck(task, SCHED_RR | SCHED_RESET_ON_FORK, &param)` the stock calls `trace_qs_set_rt_sched(task, SCHED_RR, prio)` (cold inline tracepoint block, read from the disassembly at +0x5ec); ours had only the skip trace. With it: stock 400 insns, ours 399 (was 358; 52 -> 2 multiset diff), the 5th inline tracepoint block and 5 alternative sites appeared (.altinstructions 252 = 252, was 246).
- `trace_qs_set_vip_sched(from, to, 5, to_qos)` takes the CONSTANT 5 as vip argument in `qos_set_callback` and `qos_reset_callback` (stock `mov w3,#5`), but `data->vip_prio` in `qos_inherit_callback` and `restore_qos_sched` (verified per function: the wrong choice makes those two worse, 6 -> 27 and 33 -> 58).
- `fair_policy(policy)` (`NORMAL || BATCH`, `cmp #3` first) replaces the hand-written `BATCH || NORMAL` in qos_set_callback: the policy csel matches now. `struct sched_param param` is declared INSIDE the blocks that use it in qos_set_callback / restore_qos_sched / qos_reset_callback (the kernel is built with -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero: a function-level declaration forces a `str wzr` at entry, the stock has none): reset 7 -> 6 diff, restore 33 -> 32.
- State (multiset diff vs stock, real Kleaf build): qos_set_callback 2, qos_inherit_callback 6 (`cbz w; cmp #3` test order, frame), qos_reset_callback 6, restore_qos_sched 32, qievent_callback 33, set_rtg_grp 153 (801 vs 815 insns). The last three are the known `g_draw_grp` clear-loop forms (stock pre-indexed `mov x11,x8; ldr x10,[x11,#0x14]!` + shared `str xzr,[x11]` tail) and the draw-table state-machine layout; unchanged this round (the same pre-index shape appears in xr_qi wq_add: both are the DAGCombiner pre-index of a GEP that is used again later, not controllable from C so far). Nothing else is missing: all 16 trace events and the 24 logic functions have the full recovered semantics.
- Tools: `g1q2_tools/` (see the xr_qi STATUS), scratch <work-dir> package `re/xr_qs_g1q2`.
"""

for mod, first, section in (("xr_qi", QI_FIRST, QI_SECTION), ("xr_qs", QS_FIRST, QS_SECTION)):
    p = mod + "/STATUS.md"
    b = open(p, "rb").read().decode("utf8")
    nl = "\r\n" if "\r\n" in b else "\n"
    lines = b.split(nl)
    assert lines[0].startswith("# " + mod), lines[0][:40]
    out = first + nl + section.replace("\n", nl).rstrip(nl) + nl + nl.join(lines[1:])
    open(p, "wb").write(out.encode("utf8"))
    print(mod, "CRLF" if nl == "\r\n" else "LF", len(out))
